<Base title="Privacy — TenLing" description="How TenLing handles your documents and settings.">
  <main id="main" class="prose opening">
    <h1>Privacy.</h1>
    <p>Effective September 28, 2026.</p>
    <h2>Your documents stay with you.</h2>
    <p>TenLing is a local Markdown editor. It does not require an account, include advertising, or send your documents to our servers. We do not collect analytics or track you across apps and websites.</p>
    <h2>Files and preferences</h2>
    <p>The app reads and writes documents and images you choose. Recent-file paths, file-access bookmarks, appearance, and keyboard preferences are stored on your device. Files saved to iCloud Drive or another file provider are handled by that provider according to its privacy policy.</p>
    <h2>Network connections</h2>
    <p>The direct desktop edition can contact GitHub to check for and download updates. App Store editions use Apple's update system. Opening a link launches your browser or another app; that destination's privacy policy applies. Pasted images may be read from their source to save them with your document.</p>
    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>If you contact us or file an issue, the information you choose to share is used to answer your request. Please do not include private document contents in public issues.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/SihanTeng/tenling/issues">Contact support</a></p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This website is hosted on Cloudflare and loads fonts from Google Fonts. Those services receive ordinary web requests, which can include your IP address. The app does not load these website fonts.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
